{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21Spectrum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21Spectrum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Determinant.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.SeminormalV21Trace"],"declarations":36,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.ladder_phase_vanishes_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.ladder_phase_vanishes_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L302-L305","doc":"The ladder phase vanishes at `q = 1` for **any** Markov parameter, `z_C` and\n`z_D` alike — it is `h` that vanishes, not `z − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.trace_sigma1_mul_sigma2inv_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.trace_sigma1_mul_sigma2inv_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L298-L300","doc":"The elliptic character at `q = 1` is `−1`, i.e. `2cos α = −1`, `α = 2π/3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.hq_one_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.hq_one_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L293-L296","doc":"**The classical limits differ.**  At `q = 1` the elliptic character is `−1`,\nso its eigenphase is `2π/3`; the ladder phase `α = (z−1)h/2` vanishes there,\nbecause `h(1) = 0`.  They do not even share a `q → 1` limit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.trace_sigma1_mul_sigma2inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.trace_sigma1_mul_sigma2inv","kind":"theorem","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L281-L291","doc":"**`trace (σ₁σ₂⁻¹) = −1 − h²`** — a genuinely `q`-dependent character, so the\nrepresentation is not short of oscillatory phases.  It is elliptic exactly when\n`h² ≤ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.sigma1_mul_sigma2inv_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.sigma1_mul_sigma2inv_eq","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L272-L279","doc":"The explicit product `σ₁σ₂⁻¹`, mirroring `Seminormal.sigma1_mul_sigma2_eq`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.det_sigma1_mul_sigma2inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.det_sigma1_mul_sigma2inv","kind":"theorem","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L261-L270","doc":"`det (σ₁σ₂⁻¹) = 1`: an even-length word, so it meets the determinant half. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.sigma2_mul_sigma2inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.sigma2_mul_sigma2inv","kind":"theorem","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L250-L259","doc":"It really is the inverse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.sigma2inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.sigma2inv","kind":"def","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L245-L248","doc":"The explicit inverse of `σ₂` (built from `det σ₂ = −1`, so no `Matrix.inv`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.zC_ne_seminormal_d1_at_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.zC_ne_seminormal_d1_at_four","kind":"theorem","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L234-L241","doc":"**Convention C does not have that property.**  At `q = 4`,\n`z_C = √4/(4+1) = 2/5` while `d₁ = 64/17`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.zD_add_d2_eq_h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.zD_add_d2_eq_h","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L225-L232","doc":"**Convention D splits the Hecke differential across the `V_(2,1)` diagonal**:\n`z_D + d₂ = h`.  The two seminormal diagonal entries of `σ₂` are `z_D` and\n`h − z_D`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.zD_eq_seminormal_d1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.zD_eq_seminormal_d1","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L221-L223","doc":"**`z_D` IS the seminormal `σ₂` diagonal entry `d₁`** — the same rational\nfunction, not a numerical coincidence at one anchor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.zD","kind":"def","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L218-L219","doc":"Convention-D Markov parameter `z_D = q³/(q²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.Delta_beta_central","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.Delta_beta_central","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L206-L214","doc":"**`Δ_β` is scalar, so its spectrum is a repeated real eigenvalue.**  Stated\nas: it commutes with every `2×2` matrix — the defining property of a scalar, and\nthe reason it cannot carry a nontrivial pair of eigenphases. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.not_unitCirclePair_Delta_beta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.not_unitCirclePair_Delta_beta","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L197-L204","doc":"**`Δ_β` carries a unit-circle pair only if `h = ±2`.**  Contrapositively: at\nany `q` with `h(q)² ≠ 4` — the substrate included, where `h ≈ 0.209` — the only\n`M_β` the corpus defines has no eigenphase. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.not_unitCirclePair_T_mix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.not_unitCirclePair_T_mix","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L189-L195","doc":"**`T_mix` carries no unit-circle pair, for any real `q`.**  Its determinant\nis `−(1 + h²/4) ≤ −1 < 1`, so the exclusion is uniform in `q` rather than an\naccident of the substrate value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.not_unitCirclePair_T_nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.not_unitCirclePair_T_nn","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L184-L187","doc":"`T_nn` carries no unit-circle pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.not_unitCirclePair_T_pp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.not_unitCirclePair_T_pp","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L179-L182","doc":"`T_pp` carries no unit-circle pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.not_unitCirclePair_of_det_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.not_unitCirclePair_of_det_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L170-L175","doc":"A matrix whose determinant is not `1` carries no unit-circle pair, for any\n`α` whatsoever. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.unitCirclePair_discriminant_nonpos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.unitCirclePair_discriminant_nonpos","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L165-L168","doc":"The discriminant is nonpositive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.unitCirclePair_discriminant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.unitCirclePair_discriminant","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L157-L163","doc":"**Why the pair is genuinely non-real**: the characteristic discriminant of\n`X² − 2cos α·X + 1` is `−(2 sin α)² ≤ 0`, so the roots are a conjugate pair on\nthe unit circle rather than two reals (they coincide exactly when `sin α = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.UnitCirclePair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.UnitCirclePair","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L153-L155","doc":"`M` carries the unit-circle pair `{e^{±iα}}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.det_Delta_beta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.det_Delta_beta","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L136-L144","doc":"`det Δ_β = h²/4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.det_T_mix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.det_T_mix","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L126-L134","doc":"`det T_mix = −(1 + h²/4)`.  Strictly below `−1` over an ordered field, so it\nis never `1` — `T_mix` is excluded for **every** `q`, not merely at the substrate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.det_T_nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.det_T_nn","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L122-L124","doc":"`det T_nn = −1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.det_T_pp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.det_T_pp","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L118-L120","doc":"`det T_pp = −1` (Hecke unimodularity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.Delta_beta_universal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.Delta_beta_universal","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L109-L114","doc":"**The universality claim**: the `nn → mix` and `mix → pp` steps give the same\nmatrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.Delta_beta_eq_scalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.Delta_beta_eq_scalar","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L101-L107","doc":"**`Δ_β = (h/2)·I`** — the boxed proposition of `prop:beta-decay-transfer-matrix`,\nderived from the entries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.T_mix_midpoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.T_mix_midpoint","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L94-L99","doc":"`T_mix` is the midpoint of the two group elements. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.T_pp_mul_T_nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.T_pp_mul_T_nn","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L87-L92","doc":"**`T_nn` is the inverse of `T_pp`**, so the block's `(1, −h)` convention is\nforced exactly as it claims. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.T_pp_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.T_pp_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L78-L85","doc":"**`T_pp` satisfies the Hecke relation** `σ² = h·σ + 1`.  So its eigenvalues\nare the Hecke eigenvalues `q` and `−q⁻¹`, and it really is the `V_(2,1)` action\nof a generator rather than an unrelated `2×2` matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.Delta_beta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.Delta_beta","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L75-L76","doc":"The universal beta decay matrix `Δ_β := T_mix − T_nn`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.T_mix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.T_mix","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L71-L73","doc":"`T_mix = T(1, −h/2) = ½(σ + σ⁻¹)`: an algebraic average, **not** a group\nelement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.T_nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.T_nn","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L68-L69","doc":"`T_nn = T(1, −h)`; represents `σ⁻¹`, per the block's uniqueness remark. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.T_pp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.T_pp","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L65-L66","doc":"`T_pp = T(1, 0)`; represents `σ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.betaT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.betaT","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L61-L63","doc":"The crossing transfer matrix `T(c,d) = !![c·h + d, c; c, d]` of\n`prop:beta-decay-transfer-matrix`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.hq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MBetaV21.hq","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MBetaV21Spectrum.lean#L58-L59","doc":"Hecke differential `h(q) = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}